    },
    {
      "$type": "prop",
      "name": "data-sort-field",
      "type": "string",
      "observed": true,
      "declared": true,
      "kind": "style",
      "description": "current sort (asc | desc)"
    },
    {
      "$type": "prop",
      "name": "data-total-pages",
      "type": "number",
      "observed": true,
      "declared": true,
      "kind": "style",
      "description": "how many pages the host believes there are. The grid reads it and never writes it: a Find steps past the last page by it, and a count that has not changed is not reported again, so the echo of its own report cannot loop. JS API — what a person can do by clicking, a caller can do by calling. This is what lets a SAVED VIEW, a preset or an agent configure a grid: setColumnFilter(field, clause)  set one column's filter from a store FilterClause columnClause(field)            read it back — the same clause, for saving suspendColumnFilter(field, on) keep the clause but stop applying it clearColumnFilter(field?)      delete one, or all openColumnFilter(field, anchor) open that column's menu, anchored anywhere select(keys) / clearSelection() set the selection BY KEY (needs `key` in populate) actionsFor(count)              the actions that apply to a selection of that size — all of them for 1, only the `multi` ones for 2+, none for 0. A bulk toolbar reads this so it cannot disagree with the row menu selectedKeys / selectedRecords read it back"
    }
  ],
